# Decision records

{% if project_name %}Decisions taken in {{ project_name }}, newest last.
{%- else %}Decisions taken in this project, newest last.
{%- endif %}

A record captures a decision that was expensive to reach and would otherwise be
re-litigated: what forced it, what was chosen, and what the choice costs. Something
obvious in hindsight still earns one when the reasoning is not obvious from the code.

Copy `0000-template.md` to the next number. Numbers are never reused, and a decision that
no longer holds gets a new record superseding the old rather than an edit, so the history
of what was believed stays readable.

A decision held as a beads `decision` bead needs no copy. `render_adrs.py` writes its
record and its row below at pre-commit, once the bead is closed. The rows between the
markers are generated from the database, and everything outside them is this project's
to edit.

